that I can do really cool stuff
with BigQuery, with nested

00:36:05.640 --> 00:36:06.840
and repeated fields.

00:36:06.840 --> 00:36:10.530
So let me just make sure that I
cover some of the key takeaways

00:36:10.530 --> 00:36:12.060
from what Evan said.

00:36:12.060 --> 00:36:13.990
And Evan can keep
me honest here.

00:36:13.990 --> 00:36:17.660
So the first thing to remember
about arrays in BigQuery, there

00:36:17.660 --> 00:36:21.560
are these lists that can have
zero or many values, right?

00:36:21.560 --> 00:36:23.820
They're ordered lists of items.

00:36:23.820 --> 00:36:28.860
But all the values in the array
must have the same data type.

00:36:28.860 --> 00:36:31.710
You could have arrays of
integers, strings, and so on,

00:36:31.710 --> 00:36:33.744
right, very important.

00:36:33.744 --> 00:36:35.910
And the other point that
you need to remember, here,

00:36:35.910 --> 00:36:38.070
when you are talking
about the arrays,

00:36:38.070 --> 00:36:42.030
these are SQL 2011
arrays, standard arrays.

00:36:42.030 --> 00:36:43.650
All right, so that was arrays.

00:36:43.650 --> 00:36:46.500
Let's move forward and
talk about the structs.

00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:47.760
So what are structs?

00:36:47.760 --> 00:36:51.370
So structs can have many
different data types.

00:36:51.370 --> 00:36:55.180
You can have structs with
integers, structs with strings.

00:36:55.180 --> 00:36:59.310
You can even have structs
with arrays, right?

00:36:59.310 --> 00:37:02.340
Remember, you cannot have
arrays inside of arrays.

00:37:02.340 --> 00:37:04.887
But you can have arrays
inside of struts.

00:37:04.887 --> 00:37:06.720
And if you're wondering
about the connection

00:37:06.720 --> 00:37:09.900
here to the SQL 2011
standards, these structs

00:37:09.900 --> 00:37:13.180
are SQL 2011 structured types.

00:37:13.180 --> 00:37:17.250
All right, so I hope this
makes sense to Evan so far.

00:37:17.250 --> 00:37:19.580
I think it makes sense to me.

00:37:19.580 --> 00:37:23.150
And this is where I had my,
what I call, an Inception style

00:37:23.150 --> 00:37:26.090
moment, when I understood
these nested and repeated

00:37:26.090 --> 00:37:28.010
fields in BigQuery.

00:37:28.010 --> 00:37:31.190
They're just arrays
containing structs

00:37:31.190 --> 00:37:34.130
that may have arrays inside
of them with other structs,

00:37:34.130 --> 00:37:37.230
with other structs, and
arrays, and so forth.

00:37:37.230 --> 00:37:41.560
So as it's called, sometimes
it's turtles all the way down.

00:37:41.560 --> 00:37:43.730
OK, so that was
the key takeaway.

00:37:43.730 --> 00:37:45.860
We have these structs in arrays.

00:37:45.860 --> 00:37:48.410
Now, let's think about
what this means in context

00:37:48.410 --> 00:37:50.410
of this Hacker News data set.

